all right today i have a sponsored video  we partnered with a project called  interlude to make this video so i'll  take a few minutes to tell you about  what they're all about it's a  convergence of blockchain technology and  pc gaming blockchain has been  implemented in games in some interesting  ways and what interlude is doing with  blockchain is very outside the box and  worth checking out so interlude is a  blockchain based gaming protocol that is  used collaboratively by thousands of  independent developers in a  decentralized way  interlude lets game developers take the  games they created  and connect them to thousands of other  independently developed pc games games  which would otherwise be unrelated  interlude is the technology that  connects the games and so why would we  want to do that here's why  interlude allows developers to hide a  virtual key somewhere in their game so  that the player can find the key it only  takes the developer a minute to do this  using a really simple interface  the condition for the player to find the  key can vary could be reaching a level  beating a boss  each key from every game in the entire  interlude network is stored on the  interlude blockchain smart contract and  in these games when a player finds a key  the interlude smart contract tells the  player what game to play next in order  to find the next key all the keys are in  order so the whole point of interlude is  it's a scavenger hunt across a whole  network of games creating really like a  meta game the entire ecosystem of the  game  is powered by its native token the shell  or ish which is  minted on the interlude smart contract  when a key is found in a game and the  shell tokens are shared between the  players and developers as rewards for  completing scavenger hunts so what's  cool about this is that the developers  and the players are working together on  an ongoing basis to make that interlude  metagame happen  with totally decentralized dynamics with  interlude players and developers are  connected through the blockchain and  everyone's playing a role in the  scavenger hunt completely permissionless  and it has the potential to span across  thousands of games it's a really cool  thing to get involved with on the  developer side because small independent  game developers are getting access to  things they otherwise wouldn't have when  working on their own projects things uh  that the interlude universe provides  like the meaning and purpose you feel  from contributing to a larger world with  tons of human players as well as your  potential  to monetize your game through the shell  tokens monetization is a huge issue for  small independent game developers now on  the player side there's a bunch of  different ways that this is appealing  you can play the games you were going to  play anyway but you can use interlude to  elevate your games to a larger  interconnected experience where you're  joining a community of people doing the  same thing and you can discover awesome  indie games that you may not have  otherwise stumbled upon this past august  interlude did their first ever demo  scavenger hunt was a big success there  were four keys in four games each key  made very quickly by a single developer  there were more than 500 players  involved over 50 people finished the  scavenger hunt the next scavenger hunt  is happening sunday october 3rd  big prize for the winner this scavenger  hunt will feature five keys  hidden in five games and this time  instead of all the games being by the  same developer the games for this event  were made by separate game developers so  this is the first event  bringing together bringing to life  interlude's vision for decentralized  game design proving you can get awesome  meta gameplay from a group of games made  by developers who have nothing to do  with each other all enabled by  interludes technology interlude's  long-term goal  is to create a massive scavenger hunt  network with thousands of games with  millions of different possible scavenger  hunt variations the whole concept of  interconnecting games in this way  is one that has not been explored enough  and interlude is doing it in a really  fresh way using blockchain for exactly  the type of thing blockchain is perfect  for check out interlude i've put a link  to their website right underneath this  video you can get involved as a player  you can get involved as a developer you  can check out what's going on with shell  the platform's token interlude is on  twitter and telegram and other socials  their communities getting bigger all the  time there are always a lot of exciting  new updates as the project continues  picking up steam and thanks to interlude  for partnering with us on this video the  team is cool we've enjoyed working with  them to help get the word out about this  fun and unique project and of course  anytime money is at play  make sure you're doing your due  diligence and understanding  the decisions you're making about money  always important never making a  financial recommendation on the program
 

